  "prefLabel": "Pda 510.02 Display of Mooring Permit Name and Number",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pda 510.02 Display of Mooring Permit Name and Number. The mooring permit holder shall write in permanent ink his or her last name, if an individual, or the name of the business organization, trust or not-for-profit entity, as applicable, and the mooring permit number on the mooring buoy in letters and numbers at least 2 inches in size above the water line, to ensure visibility.\n\nSource. #7940, eff 8-23-03; ss by #9975, eff 8-20-11 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Pda 500); ss by #12958, eff 12-24-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pda100-700.html"
